<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>ASIK Aggregation | DevOps Deployment</title>

    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a, #1e3a8a);
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 80px auto;
            padding: 40px;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 48px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .subtitle {
            font-size: 20px;
            color: #cbd5e1;
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }

        .card {
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
            border-radius: 16px;
            padding: 30px;
            margin-bottom: 25px;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
        }

        .tools {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 15px;
            margin-top: 25px;
        }

        .tool {
            background: white;
            color: #0f172a;
            padding: 12px 20px;
            border-radius: 25px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .pipeline {
            font-size: 18px;
            line-height: 2;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .success {
            color: #4ade80;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        footer {
            margin-top: 40px;
            color: #94a3b8;
            font-size: 14px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>🚀 ASIK Aggregation Service</h1>

    <div class="subtitle">
        Automated CI/CD Deployment using Modern DevOps Tools
    </div>

    <div class="card">

        <h2>⚙️ DevOps Deployment Pipeline</h2>

        <div class="pipeline">
            👨‍💻 VS Code
            →
            🐙 Git
            →
            🐙 GitHub
            →
            🔨 Jenkins
            →
            🐳 Docker
            →
            ☁️ AWS ECR
            →
            ⚙️ Ansible
            →
            🚀 Application Server
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="card">

        <h2>🛠️ Technologies Used</h2>

        <div class="tools">

            <div class="tool">VS Code</div>
            <div class="tool">Git</div>
            <div class="tool">GitHub</div>
            <div class="tool">Jenkins</div>
            <div class="tool">Docker</div>
            <div class="tool">Ansible</div>
            <div class="tool">AWS</div>
            <div class="tool">Amazon ECR</div>
            <div class="tool">Linux</div>

        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="card">

        <h2>🔄 CI/CD Workflow</h2>

        <p>
            Source code is developed in <strong>VS Code</strong> and
            version-controlled using <strong>Git</strong>.
        </p>

        <p>
            Code is pushed to <strong>GitHub</strong>, triggering the
            <strong>Jenkins CI/CD pipeline</strong>.
        </p>

        <p>
            Jenkins builds the application into a
            <strong>Docker image</strong> and pushes it to
            <strong>AWS Elastic Container Registry (ECR)</strong>.
        </p>

        <p>
            <strong>Ansible</strong> then pulls the image from ECR,
            removes the previous container, deploys the new container,
            and verifies the deployment.
        </p>

        <p class="success">
            ✅ Deployment Completed Successfully
        </p>

    </div>

    <div class="card">

        <h2>☁️ AWS Infrastructure</h2>

        <p>
            Hosted on <strong>AWS EC2</strong> with Docker-based application
            deployment and <strong>Amazon ECR</strong> for container image
            management.
        </p>

        <p>
            The complete deployment process is automated through
            Jenkins and Ansible.
        </p>

    </div>

    <footer>
        ASIK Aggregation Service | Automated DevOps CI/CD Pipeline
        <br>
        Git • GitHub • Jenkins • Docker • Ansible • AWS • ECR
    </footer>

</div>

</body>
</html>